  "result": "Fixed! The bug was in line 69 of `/src/server/services/search-service.ts`. The condition was inverted—it was rejecting queries with colons when `advanced` was `true` (meaning the feature IS enabled) when it should reject them when `advanced` is `false` (meaning the feature is NOT enabled).\n\nChanged:\n```typescript\nif (input.q.includes(\":\") && advanced) {\n```\n\nTo:\n```typescript\nif (input.q.includes(\":\") && !advanced) {\n```\n\nNow customers with field-scoped search in their plan can use colon syntax freely, while those without it will see the error message as intended.",
